{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-bd6e9220-c156-4f57-8200-347a59c401d9","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-83dbd54cf2ffc572","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-g6rwamj0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-E002.md","content":"# Enable the pgvector remote vector_io provider in OGX\n\n## Description\n\nThis epic delivers the OGX-side integration that makes a PostgreSQL instance with pgvector usable as the remote vector store for Gen AI Studio playground RAG. The existing remote vector store implementation is largely reusable for pgvector — the majority of the strategy's effort is in infrastructure and provisioning, not the vector_io provider integration itself — so this epic adapts and validates that implementation for the pgvector backend and documents the configuration surface that downstream consumers (the gen-ai BFF creating OGXServer instances) wire against.\n\nThe vector store must run as a separate process, decoupled from the OGX instance (not an inline provider), replacing the reliance on the inline Milvus provider that is being removed from the Llama Stack distribution for GA readiness.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Adapt and verify the existing remote vector store implementation for the pgvector backend, activated through the OGX vector_io provider configuration (`remote::pgvector` via its `ENABLE_PGVECTOR` environment guard).\n- Support supplying the PostgreSQL connection details through secret-backed configuration, suitable for per-namespace scoping in multi-tenant environments.\n- Verify vector I/O operations (vector store registration, document insertion, and retrieval/query) against a PostgreSQL instance with pgvector enabled, exercising the provider end to end.\n- Keep OGX's application storage backend configuration (key-value and SQL storage) entirely untouched — it remains on its existing default; vector storage and application storage are independent configurations and no storage migration is in scope.\n- Document the provider configuration surface (environment variables and secret references) that consumers use when wiring OGXServer instances.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The pgvector vector_io provider activates when configured, and vector register/insert/query operations succeed against a pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance.\n- The vector store runs as a separate process decoupled from the OGX process — no inline vector provider is used.\n- OGX's application storage backend remains on its existing default configuration; no application-storage migration is performed or required.\n- The provider configuration surface (activation guard, connection/secret references) is documented for the consumers that will configure OGXServer instances.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **AC-2 (playground RAG workflows function with the default vector store, no loss of current capability):** this epic delivers the provider capability that the playground RAG workflows will exercise end to end.\n- **AC-4 (default vector store runs as a separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance):** delivered by enabling the remote pgvector provider rather than an inline provider.\n- **AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation):** the provider's connection configuration supports per-namespace scoped instances.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":73885,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-beca486d0051d478","agent_id":"a62e85b504ccecffb","session_id":"95b0e417-f5cf-489c-8110-90a1ec4486c8","uuid":"76f42d86-efe7-4d60-99ce-cfc8419d7f4d","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:41:41.168Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
