{"type":"assistant","message":{"id":"chatcmpl-9230dbf8-2a66-4450-8e4d-e52f89b61f58","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"chatcmpl-tool-8322afd4802a3178","name":"Write","input":{"file_path":"/private/var/folders/h5/l8qslbp55w5621qf9ngsh5jc0000gn/T/epic-RHAISTRAT-8004-g6rwamj0/artifacts/epic-tasks/RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004.md","content":"# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio\n\n## Description\n\nBranch A of the provisioning decision: if the go/no-go selects operator-based self-provisioning, this epic implements PostgreSQL lifecycle management in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer for Gen AI Studio — the operator layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) — following the model-registry-operator pattern for auto-provisioned databases. Each playground namespace gets a pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance reconciled by the operator, so Gen AI Studio's RAG capabilities have a default vector store out of the box without any user provisioning.\n\nThis branch is only instantiated if the RHOAI-controlled operator layer is available in time for the target release; the upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry RHOAI-specific provisioning logic, which is why the operator layer is a hard dependency.\n\n## Scope\n\n- Implement PostgreSQL instance lifecycle management in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer, following the model-registry-operator pattern: controller-created Deployment, Service, and credentials Secret per instance, with cleanup on deletion.\n- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that ships pgvector out of the box (already used by the model-registry-operator for its auto-provisioned database, and already referenced for disconnected installs) — no custom image build and no build-pipeline onboarding is required.\n- Scope instances per namespace for multi-tenant isolation.\n- Set PostgreSQL resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's reference sizing, adjusted based on benchmark results.\n- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DSC becomes available (planned RHOAI 3.6), consumers switch to the shared connection string instead of self-provisioned instances — the provisioning must not become a permanent fixture.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- The operator reconciles namespace-scoped PostgreSQL instances with pgvector available, including credential management via Secret and cleanup when the owning resource is deleted.\n- No custom container image is built or onboarded; the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector is used.\n- Instances run with resource requests/limits derived from the model-registry-operator reference, and the default instance profile is lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments.\n- Portability is documented: switching to the platform-provided shared database requires only consuming its connection string, with no change to the vector store consumption path.\n- Per-namespace isolation is verified: instances in different namespaces serve isolated vector store data.\n\n## HLR Traceability\n\n- **AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning):** this branch delivers the out-of-the-box provisioning when operator-based self-provisioning is selected.\n- **AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance):** the PostgreSQL workload is reconciled as its own deployment, decoupled from the OGX instance.\n- **AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation):** instances are scoped per namespace.\n- **AC-6 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments):** reference-based resource sizing with benchmark adjustment.\n- **SC-2 (no additional manual setup steps):** operator reconciliation removes all user-side setup.\n"}}],"model":"rits/zai-org/glm-5-3","stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":75710,"output_tokens":0},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-beca486d0051d478","agent_id":"a62e85b504ccecffb","session_id":"95b0e417-f5cf-489c-8110-90a1ec4486c8","uuid":"45007bb3-6ce5-43a3-8284-38fe7c7d86d9","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:42:06.097Z","subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Decompose RHAISTRAT-8004"}
