ied. |\n12\t| repo_access | 0 | The current odh-dashboard repository is accessible, but the modularized operator layout this epic targets is defined by in-flight work (RHAISTRAT-7164); where the new code lands is not yet determinable. |\n13\t| architecture_claims | 1 | The epic's premise — that a platform operator can auto-provision per-instance PostgreSQL following the model-registry-operator pattern, and that a Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector already exists — is corroborated by `.context/architecture-context/architecture/rhoai-3.6-ea.1/model-registry-operator.md`, which documents exactly that provisioning pattern (per-instance postgres Deployments, Secrets, Services on port 5432). |\n14\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-94f4f2b0b8f7c7fb","agent_id":"aa80cc8176649b2fd","session_id":"95b0e417-f5cf-489c-8110-90a1ec4486c8","uuid":"878cd89a-ea52-433c-bd0e-6231d0d89bcc","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:48:20.749Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-8fece184ac1684f8","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Revise RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
