{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-adbfe2daf6c40514","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tepic_id: RHAISTRAT-8004-BRANCH-A-E004\n3\ttitle: Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio\n4\tparent_strat: RHAISTRAT-8004\n5\tcomponent: Gen AI Studio\n6\tteam: Gen AI Studio\n7\ttype: Implementation\n8\tpriority: P0\n9\tbranch: A\n10\tgated_by: RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n11\tdependencies:\n12\t- RHAISTRAT-8004-E001\n13\tgate_failure_impact:\n14\t  action: remove\n15\t  fallback_approach: If the RHOAI-controlled operator layer from dashboard operator\n16\t    modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) does not land in time for the target release,\n17\t    this approach is removed; provisioning falls back to the BFF-managed path or,\n18\t    as last resort, to requiring customers to bring their own PostgreSQL.\n19\tai_signals:\n20\t  change_specificity: 0\n21\t  pattern_precedent: 1\n22\t  adapter_pattern: 1\n23\t  existing_foundation: -1\n24\t  open_questions: -1\n25\t  external_dependency: 1\n26\t  human_process_gates: 0\n27\t  repo_access: 0\n28\t  architecture_claims: 1\n29\timplementation_type: null\n30\tinvestigation_signals: null\n31\tai_implementability: Medium\n32\tai_implementability_score: 2\n33\tjira_key: null\n34\t---\n35\t# Operator-based PostgreSQL/pgvector provisioning for Gen AI Studio\n36\t\n37\t## Description\n38\t\n39\tBranch A of the provisioning decision: if the go/no-go selects operator-based self-provisioning, this epic implements PostgreSQL lifecycle management in the RHOAI-controlled operator layer for Gen AI Studio — the operator layer delivered by the dashboard operator modularization (RHAISTRAT-7164) — following the model-registry-operator pattern for auto-provisioned databases. Each playground namespace gets a pgvector-enabled PostgreSQL instance reconciled by the operator, so Gen AI Studio's RAG capabilities have a default vector store out of the box without any user provisioning.\n40\t\n41\tThis branch is only instantiated if the RHOAI-controlled operator layer is available in time for the target release; the upstream ogx-k8s-operator cannot carry RHOAI-specific provisioning logic, which is why the operator layer is a hard dependency.\n42\t\n43\t## Scope\n44\t\n45\t- Implement PostgreSQL instance lifecycle management in the RHOAI-controlled Gen AI Studio operator layer, following the model-registry-operator pattern: controller-created Deployment, Service, and credentials Secret per instance, with cleanup on deletion.\n46\t- Use the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image that ships pgvector out of the box (already used by the model-registry-operator for its auto-provisioned database, and already referenced for disconnected installs) — no custom image build and no build-pipeline onboarding is required.\n47\t- Scope instances per namespace for multi-tenant isolation.\n48\t- Set PostgreSQL resource requests/limits starting from the model-registry-operator's reference sizing, adjusted based on benchmark results.\n49\t- Design for portability: when the platform-provided shared PostgreSQL managed via the DSC becomes available (planned RHOAI 3.6), consumers switch to the shared connection string instead of self-provisioned instances — the provisioning must not become a permanent fixture.\n50\t\n51\t## Acceptance Criteria\n52\t\n53\t- The operator reconciles namespace-scoped PostgreSQL instances with pgvector available, including credential management via Secret and cleanup when the owning resource is deleted.\n54\t- No custom container image is built or onboarded; the existing Red Hat PostgreSQL image with pgvector is used.\n55\t- Instances run with resource requests/limits derived from the model-registry-operator reference, and the default instance profile is lightweight enough for resource-constrained environments.\n56\t- Portability is documented: switching to the platform-provided shared database requires only consuming its connection string, with no change to the vector store consumption path.\n57\t- Per-namespace isolation is verified: instances in different namespaces serve isolated vector store data.\n58\t\n59\t## HLR Traceability\n60\t\n61\t- **AC-1 (default vector store available out-of-the-box, no manual provisioning):** this branch delivers the out-of-the-box provisioning when operator-based self-provisioning is selected.\n62\t- **AC-4 (separate process, decoupled from the Llama Stack instance):** the PostgreSQL workload is reconciled as its own deployment, decoupled from the OGX instance.\n63\t- **AC-5 (multi-tenant scoping, per-namespace isolation):** instances are scoped per namespace.\n64\t- **AC-6 (lightweight for resource-constrained environments):** reference-based resource sizing with benchmark adjustment.\n65\t- **SC-2 (no additional manual setup steps):** operator reconciliation removes all user-side setup.\n66\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"chatcmpl-tool-9fab0a6e3589f71b","agent_id":"aa3d9f1d9fb68bac1","session_id":"95b0e417-f5cf-489c-8110-90a1ec4486c8","uuid":"cb48d5d5-afba-4852-8193-71069e18589e","timestamp":"2026-10-26T11:50:27.073Z","tool_result_meta":[{"id":"chatcmpl-tool-adbfe2daf6c40514","permission_decision":{"decision":"accept","source":"config","reason_type":"mode"}}],"subagent_type":"general-purpose","task_description":"Re-review RHAISTRAT-8004 decomposition"}
